# UI Component Standards with Atlaskit

## Design System Principles

### Atlassian Design System Integration
This project uses [Atlassian's Design System](https://atlassian.design/) and [Atlaskit](https://atlaskit.atlassian.com/) as the primary UI component library for:
- **Design with Clarity**: Following Atlassian's design principles for clear, confident interfaces
- **Foundational Guidelines**: Using design tokens and modular building blocks
- **Accessibility**: Built-in accessibility features enabling everyone to interact and navigate
- **Theme Support**: Native light and dark mode support with design tokens
- **Professional Quality**: Enterprise-grade components with consistent experiences
- **TypeScript Support**: Full TypeScript definitions included

### Atlassian Design Foundations
All UI components should follow [Atlassian's Design System](https://atlassian.design/) foundations:

#### Design Tokens
- **Single sources of truth** to name and store design decisions
- **Spacing tokens** for consistent layout and spacing
- **Color tokens** for brand distinction and consistent experiences
- **Typography tokens** for enhanced communication and brand reinforcement
- **Elevation tokens** for proper layering and depth

#### Visual Style Guidelines
- **Clear, concise, and conversational** language following content standards
- **Accessibility-first** design enabling everyone to interact and understand
- **Modular building blocks** for flexible component composition
- **Responsive design** patterns for all screen sizes
- **Consistent visual hierarchy** using typography and spacing

### Light & Dark Mode Support
All components must support both light and dark modes:
- Use Atlaskit's built-in theme system
- Implement proper contrast ratios for accessibility
- Test components in both light and dark themes
- Provide smooth transitions between themes

## Atlaskit Setup

### Installation
Install the core Atlaskit components following [Atlassian's component guidelines](https://atlassian.design/components):
```bash
# Core components
npm install @atlaskit/button @atlaskit/textfield @atlaskit/card @atlaskit/badge @atlaskit/flag @atlaskit/box @atlaskit/inline @atlaskit/stack

# Theme and styling
npm install @atlaskit/theme @atlaskit/theme-provider

# Additional components as needed
npm install @atlaskit/modal-dialog @atlaskit/dropdown-menu @atlaskit/tabs @atlaskit/tooltip
```

### Theme Provider Setup
```typescript
// src/components/ThemeProvider.tsx
'use client';

import { ThemeProvider as AtlaskitThemeProvider } from '@atlaskit/theme-provider';
import { createContext, useContext, useEffect, useState } from 'react';

type Theme = 'light' | 'dark' | 'auto';

type ThemeProviderProps = {
  children: React.ReactNode;
  defaultTheme?: Theme;
  storageKey?: string;
};

type ThemeProviderState = {
  theme: Theme;
  setTheme: (theme: Theme) => void;
};

const initialState: ThemeProviderState = {
  theme: 'auto',
  setTheme: () => null,
};

const ThemeProviderContext = createContext<ThemeProviderState>(initialState);

export function ThemeProvider({
  children,
  defaultTheme = 'auto',
  storageKey = 'ui-theme',
  ...props
}: ThemeProviderProps) {
  const [theme, setTheme] = useState<Theme>(defaultTheme);

  useEffect(() => {
    const root = window.document.documentElement;
    root.classList.remove('light', 'dark');

    if (theme === 'auto') {
      const systemTheme = window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)')
        .matches ? 'dark' : 'light';
      root.classList.add(systemTheme);
      return;
    }

    root.classList.add(theme);
  }, [theme]);

  const value = {
    theme,
    setTheme: (theme: Theme) => {
      localStorage.setItem(storageKey, theme);
      setTheme(theme);
    },
  };

  return (
    <ThemeProviderContext.Provider {...props} value={value}>
      <AtlaskitThemeProvider mode={theme === 'auto' ? 'light' : theme}>
        {children}
      </AtlaskitThemeProvider>
    </ThemeProviderContext.Provider>
  );
}

export const useTheme = () => {
  const context = useContext(ThemeProviderContext);

  if (context === undefined)
    throw new Error('useTheme must be used within a ThemeProvider');

  return context;
};
```

